## Approach

Replace the deprecated `query_forbidden_deps` ad-hoc path in `build_findings` with the ConstraintResolver + `set_forbidden_pairs` + `query_violations` maintained view (from 5d-3/5d-4). Enrich `ConstraintViolation` with full constraint metadata. Add constraint waiver partitioning parallel to the existing convention waiver pattern. For violation delta: use `DdEngine::update(DdDelta)` to compute which violations are introduced by edges from changed files vs pre-existing elsewhere.

Why this approach: the resolver already handles both ForbiddenDep (glob matching) and Boundary (component-based) constraint kinds, producing the `(i64, i64)` pairs the DD maintained view expects. The convention waiver pattern in lines 436-475 of review.rs is a proven template for waiver partitioning. The DdDelta approach gives precise "introduced" counts without needing baseline import data from git.

